{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-87262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.4,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.8,$ find $P({B}^{′}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-87262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.5+P(B)-0.4 \\\\ P(B) & =0.8+0.4-0.5 \\\\ P(B) & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({B}^{′}) & =1-P(B) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-87262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0b0f804b411f15c9a569944a2eb2dad8493666b6a5aa899260fa3e2331e7f145"} {"question" "q-87262" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-87262" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.3"] ["math" "0.4"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "0.7"] ["math" "0.8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-87262" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-179539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(A)=\\frac{1}{2},$ $P(B)=\\frac{2}{5},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{7}{10},$ find $P(A\\cup {B}^{′}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-179539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{7}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{5}-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{7}{10} \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A\\cup {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/assets/5ecc7dae3e6b6e57ccd4a7b8907cb4dd20b0ece400a5768b747f3cb3da788e4b.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup {B}^{′})=\\frac{3}{10}+\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-179539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0b0f804b411f15c9a569944a2eb2dad8493666b6a5aa899260fa3e2331e7f145"} {"question" "q-179539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-179539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{10}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-179539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(A)=0.25,$ $P(B)=0.45,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.6,$ find $P(A\\cup {B}^{′}).$\n\n$P(A\\cup {B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.6 & =0.25+0.45-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.25+0.45-0.6 \\\\  & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A\\cup {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/assets/f8fb716593a35fc1f85ab524dc78bf0fa0cd03dc16b0c5ca92a9b2836e6e7c5b.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup {B}^{′})=0.15+0.1+0.4=0.65.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0b0f804b411f15c9a569944a2eb2dad8493666b6a5aa899260fa3e2331e7f145"} {"question" "q-264403" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264403" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.65"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(B)=0.45,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.2,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.75,$ find $P({A}^{′}).$\n\n$P({A}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.75 & =P(A)+0.45-0.2 \\\\ P(A) & =0.75+0.2-0.45 \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-0.5 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0b0f804b411f15c9a569944a2eb2dad8493666b6a5aa899260fa3e2331e7f145"} {"question" "q-264416" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264416" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(B)=\\frac{4}{15},$ $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{15},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{4}{5},$ find $P({A}^{′}).$\n\n$P({A}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & =P(A)+\\frac{4}{15}-\\frac{1}{15} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{1}{15}-\\frac{4}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0b0f804b411f15c9a569944a2eb2dad8493666b6a5aa899260fa3e2331e7f145"} {"question" "q-264424" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"} {"question" "q-264424" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/state.json" "file_sha256" "681860361eefabe640d4f2372ca564cfaf2d69711d8a83e08183b30ebcc05de8"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2127 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
